# Line endings.
#
# Default: normalise to LF in the repository and the working tree. `core.autocrlf`
# is true on at least one machine here, and `scripts/*.sh` fail on Linux with
# "bad interpreter" under CRLF. The AIAE harness adds 22 runtime scripts and 28
# checkers to that directory in P2, so this matters beyond cosmetics.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Exception: `.claude/**` is a managed fixture tree, not our source.
#
# Every file in it is checksummed in `.claude/.aiae-fixtures-manifest`, and
# `install-managed-claude-fixtures.py:141` aborts the whole install with
# "managed fixture was edited locally; refusing overwrite" on any hash mismatch.
# There is no override flag.
#
# The manifest is *mixed*: files copied verbatim from the standard carry that
# checkout's CRLF, while files the installer rewrites through
# `rewrite-installed-documentation-paths.py` come out LF. No single line-ending
# policy can satisfy it — so git must not apply one. `-text` stores and restores
# these bytes exactly as the installer wrote them.
#
# Do not "tidy" this exemption. Normalising `.claude/**` in either direction
# breaks the manifest and blocks `install-claude-fixtures.sh` permanently,
# which P1 step 1 depends on.
.claude/** -text

# The same applies to the four root-level files the installer also owns and
# checksums (`managed_root_files` in install-managed-claude-fixtures.py:22).
# They are listed in the manifest exactly like everything under .claude/.
CLAUDE.md -text
AI-DEVELOPMENT-GUIDE.md -text
GDS-WORKFLOW-README.md -text
agent-payload.skills -text
